{"name": "b472_s1c", "sha256": "984446c82809a66a5812ff9db5d7b5c63bb95eb66e3aa416620da064b20bfb04", "words": 158, "headline": "Mostly Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 0.09619340300559998, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 0.9038066267967224, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T01:57:45Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Low", 60, 0, 360, "One of the best side-effects of learning self-hypnosis is influence literacy: an increased awareness of all the ways your attention is being shaped in your day-to-day life (a screen, a specific ad, a politician, religious fear, erotic imprinting, charismatic authority, pressure to belong, shame, a sense of urgency, repetition, etc.), and it’s all around you."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 25, 360, 495, " Sometimes it’s benign – like lullabies or prayers or being taught by a good teacher or listening to a beautiful song or being in love."], ["Human Written", "High", 79, 495, 959, " But you may want to ask yourself what effect it’s having on your ability to see clearly and make choices.\nManipulation often comes with any of the following; urgency, you are special, FOMO (fear of missing out), not be included, sexual charge, shame, confused, someone will rescue you, destiny, you should obey, secret knowledge, and an excessive sense of certainty about something way too quickly and you have a sense that one good question will break the spell."]]}
{"name": "b472_s3c", "sha256": "38950e8f882ebd5c84280e60d78997a1550b835e16d1cc477fcc3824875da5aa", "words": 152, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 2.4317075984857443e-20, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.2560425111644072e-36, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T01:57:47Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 161, 0, 831, "Then count up, using these five steps: 1...feel your body again and what it’s resting on, feel your weight (of your choice). 2...feel your breathing return to normal. 3...hear the room, name where you are. 4...wiggle your fingers and toes, move your shoulders and your eyes. 5...open your eyes, back in the here and now, feeling normal and clear. This session is now over.\nWhen you come out, remind yourself what day (or date) it is. Look to your left and your right. Look at something near, and something far. Move around a bit, and don’t get up until you feel steady. Make sure you’re truly oriented and alert (the count is supposed to bring you back, but it doesn’t always do the whole job). Take mental note of anything that has come up for you and any actions you need to take regarding it. Then go on and do something normal."]]}
